## Why This Is Asked

This question tests basic data protection practices for logging in a multi-tenant analytics platform, focusing on practical steps to prevent credential leakage without overhauling the system.

## Key Concepts

- Log redaction and sanitization
- Structured logging and ingestion pipelines
- Per-tenant data masking
- Token rotation policies
- Incident response basics for credential leakage

## Code Example

```javascript
function redactLog(event){
  try {
    const s = JSON.stringify(event);
    return s.replace(/token=[^\s&]+/gi, 'token=REDACTED');
  } catch (e) {
    return '{}';
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the log redaction in CI/CD?
- What adjustments if logs are stored in a non-text format (e.g., binary)?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, production-ready supply chain security controls across multi-cloud Kubernetes, focusing on SBOMs, artifact signing, and rapid IR.

## Key Concepts

- SBOMs and risk scoring
- Code signing with Cosign and KMS-backed keys
- CI secrets scanning
- Image-signature enforcement at admission
- 24h IR playbook and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// verify artifact signature (pseudo)
const crypto = require('crypto');
function verifySignature(blob, signature, publicKeyPem) {
  const verify = crypto.createVerify('SHA256');
  verify.update(blob);
  verify.end();
  return verify.verify(publicKeyPem, signature);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate and revoke keys in flight without downtime?
- How would you integrate Sigstore or a private CA with this workflow?

